---
import '@fontsource-variable/archivo';
import '../styles/site.css';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
const chapters = [['start','The beginning'],['tools','Better tools'],['win','A team win'],['create','More possibilities'],['about','The person']];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="Muhammad Usman Butt. Developer in Lahore building games, open-source tools, web and mobile applications. Explore the work and the story behind it."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://usmanbutt.dev/"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg"/><title>Muhammad Usman Butt · Made to interact</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/scrollcraft.css"/></head>
<body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Usman Butt, top">ub<span>↗</span></a><span class="edition">A developer's field notes<br/>Lahore, Pakistan / 2026</span><nav class="header-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/Muhammad-Usman-Butt-Resume.pdf" class="resume-top">Resume</a><a class="contact-top" href="mailto:buttu7666@gmail.com">Say hello <span>↗</span></a></nav></header>
<main id="main">
<Hero />
<div class="story-layout"><aside class="folio" aria-label="Story chapters"><p class="tiny">In this notebook</p><nav>{chapters.map(([id,label],i)=><a href={'#'+id} data-chapter-link={id}><span>0{i+1}</span>{label}</a>)}</nav><div class="grid-paper"><svg id="story-grid" viewBox="0 0 180 180" aria-hidden="true"><g class="grid-lines" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"><path d="M30 30H150V150H30ZM70 30V150M110 30V150M30 70H150M30 110H150"/></g><g class="grid-dots" fill="currentColor">{Array.from({length:9},(_,i)=><circle cx={50+(i%3)*40} cy={50+Math.floor(i/3)*40} r="5"/>)}</g><path class="grid-route" d="M50 50L130 50L90 90L50 130L130 130" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg><p id="grid-caption">A few squares. A starting point.</p></div><span class="tiny">Scroll a little. See what changes.</span></aside>
<div class="chapters">
<section id="start" class="chapter" data-sc-act="flow"><div class="chapter-label"><span>01 / The beginning</span><span>2022 →</span></div><h2>Player one.<br/>Then, developer.</h2><p class="lead">I've played games all my life. Eventually, I started building them too.</p><p>I started studying Computer Science at UMT in August 2022 and began freelance Unity work in March 2023. Alongside games, I explored the browser through small experiments in input, rules, and feedback.</p><div class="experiment"><div><span class="tiny">A small experiment</span><h3>Leave your mark.</h3><p>Click or drag across the squares.<br/>Simple inputs. Something happens.</p><button id="clear-grid" type="button">Clear the canvas ↺</button></div><div id="paint-grid" role="group" aria-label="Interactive drawing grid">{Array.from({length:64},(_,i)=><button type="button" aria-label={'Paint square '+(i+1)} aria-pressed="false"/>)}</div></div><p class="caption">Inspired by my early etch-a-sketch project. A little illustration of where curiosity can lead.</p><div class="small-links"><a href="https://usmanbutt-dev.github.io/etch-a-sketch/">Original drawing project ↗</a><a href="https://usmanbutt-dev.github.io/calculator/">Calculator ↗</a><a href="https://usmanbutt-dev.github.io/rock-paper-scissors/">Rock, paper, scissors ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="tools" class="chapter" data-sc-act="flow"><div class="chapter-label"><span>02 / Better tools</span><span>Open source</span></div><h2>Sometimes the thing<br/>to build is a better tool.</h2><p>I like the work around the work, too. The connections that make an editor easier to use, or open a new way to interact with it.</p><article class="project"><div class="project-heading"><h3>Antigravity for Unity</h3><span class="star-count" aria-label="25 GitHub stars, recorded 15 September 2026"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9733;</span><strong>25</strong><span>GitHub stars<small>Recorded 15 Sep 2026</small></span></span></div><p class="build-method"><span>Vibe-coded</span> <strong>Human-designed, AI-implemented</strong></p><p><strong class="project-summary">An open-source bridge between Unity and Antigravity.</strong> Open scripts at the right line and keep project configuration in sync.</p><figure class="artwork"><img src="/images/antigravity.png" alt="Repository artwork connecting the Unity and Antigravity symbols" width="1024" height="512" loading="lazy" data-sc-parallax="0.04"/><figcaption>Project artwork from the repository</figcaption></figure><div class="project-footer"><span>Unity Editor · C# · UPM</span><a href="https://github.com/usmanbutt-dev/antigravity-unity">Explore the repository ↗</a></div><p class="caption">*Recorded 15 September 2026.</p></article><article class="project mcp"><div class="project-heading"><h3>Unity MCP</h3><span class="status">Paused</span></div><p class="build-method"><span>Vibe-coded</span> <strong>Human-designed, AI-implemented</strong></p><p><strong class="project-summary">Tools for AI clients to inspect and work with Unity scenes, objects, and assets.</strong> I paused development when Unity introduced its own MCP tooling.</p><div class="flow-diagram" aria-label="AI client connects through MCP to Unity Editor"><span>AI client</span><b aria-hidden="true">↔</b><span>MCP</span><b aria-hidden="true">↔</b><span>Unity Editor</span></div><p class="caption">An illustration of the connection, not a running session.</p><div class="project-footer"><span>C# · JSON-RPC · Editor tooling</span><a href="https://github.com/usmanbutt-dev/unity-mcp">Read the code ↗</a></div></article></section>
<section id="win" class="chapter award" data-sc-act="flow"><div class="chapter-label"><span>03 / A team win</span><span>GIKI SOFTCOM · 2026</span></div><div class="award-number" aria-label="First place">1<span>st</span><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M50 5L60 32L88 20L74 45L98 60L69 65L72 95L50 77L27 95L31 65L3 60L26 45L12 20L40 32Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg></div><h2>Built together.<br/>First place.</h2><p class="lead">Our team won first place in Game Development at GIKI SOFTCOM in 2026.</p><p><strong class="project-summary">A one-button Unity game with attacks, gravity switching, and generated level chunks.</strong> A shared milestone in the story.</p><div class="mechanics"><span>Tap → attack</span><span>Hold → charge</span><span>Double tap → flip gravity</span></div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/usmanbutt-dev/SoftcomProject">Explore the game project ↗</a></section>
<section id="create" class="chapter" data-sc-act="flow"><div class="chapter-label"><span>04 / More possibilities</span><span>Create / extend</span></div><h2>Tools that leave<br/>room for other ideas.</h2><article class="project"><div class="project-heading"><h3>ArcSmith</h3><span class="status">Open source</span></div><p class="build-method"><span>Vibe-coded</span> <strong>Human-designed, AI-implemented</strong></p><p><strong class="project-summary">A visual narrative editor for connecting story elements.</strong> A graph workspace, project saving, undo/redo, and a local automation API support the authoring process.</p><figure class="artwork"><img src="/images/arcsmith.png" alt="ArcSmith promotional artwork showing a stylized narrative graph" width="945" height="468" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Repository promotional artwork</figcaption></figure><div class="project-footer"><span>React · TypeScript · Tauri / Rust</span><a href="https://github.com/usmanbutt-dev/ArcSmith">Explore the repository ↗</a></div></article><article class="project"><div class="project-heading"><h3>NijiStream</h3><span class="status">Extension-based app</span></div><p class="build-method"><span>Vibe-coded</span> <strong>Human-designed, AI-implemented</strong></p><p><strong class="project-summary">A media app powered by JavaScript source extensions.</strong> I used NijiStream to learn how to build an extension-based application. Its Flutter interface, library, and playback connect to JavaScript source extensions through a runtime bridge.</p><div class="extension-map"><div class="extension-core"><strong>NijiStream</strong><span>Interface · Library · Playback</span></div><div class="connector" aria-hidden="true">↕</div><div class="extension-bridge">Dart ↔ JavaScript bridge</div><div class="connector" aria-hidden="true">↕</div><div class="extension-sources"><span>Search</span><span>Details</span><span>Video sources</span></div></div><p class="caption">Architecture illustration based on the repository.</p><div class="project-footer"><span>Flutter · Dart · JavaScript · SQLite</span><a href="https://github.com/usmanbutt-dev/NijiStream">Explore the repository ↗</a></div></article><div class="resolution"><span class="tiny">Different projects. A common interest.</span><p>How we <strong>play</strong>.<br/>How we <strong>create</strong>.<br/>What happens <strong>next</strong>.</p><a href="/projects/">There’s more in the project index ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="about" class="chapter" data-sc-act="flow"><div class="chapter-label"><span>05 / The person</span><span>Lahore, Pakistan</span></div><h2>Still curious.<br/>Still building.</h2><p>I'm Muhammad Usman Butt, a software engineer with a BS in Computer Science from UMT. My work spans games and spatial experiences, web and mobile applications, and AI integrations.</p><section aria-labelledby="ai-workflow-title"><h3 id="ai-workflow-title">Working with AI</h3><p>I design the systems behind my vibe-coded projects and use AI to write the implementation. Directing that work has helped me become more confident working with coding agents and AI development workflows.</p></section><div class="experience"><div><time>Jun – Sep 2026</time><h3>Termnl Tech</h3><p><strong>AI & Full-Stack Engineer Intern</strong></p></div><div><time>Apr – Jun 2026</time><h3>Axiolink Game Studio</h3><p><strong>Head of Game Development</strong> · completed three-month role</p></div><div><time>Sep 2025 – Apr 2026</time><h3>AstroApe Studios</h3><p><strong>Unity Developer</strong></p></div><div><time>Mar 2023 →</time><h3>Freelance</h3><p><strong>Unity Developer</strong> · VR and multiplayer experiences</p></div></div><p class="caption">BS Computer Science, UMT · Aug 2022–Aug 2026 · CGPA 3.50/4.00.<br/>Game-development community work with UMT ACM and GDGoC UMT.</p><div class="closing"><span class="tiny">The next chapter</span><h2>Have a role in mind?<br/>Let's talk<span class="blue">.</span></h2><a class="email" href="mailto:buttu7666@gmail.com">buttu7666@gmail.com ↗</a><div class="small-links"><a href="/Muhammad-Usman-Butt-Resume.pdf">Resume ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/usmanbutt-dev">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/usmanbutt-dev/">LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div></section>
</div></div></main><footer class="wrap footer"><span>© 2026 Muhammad Usman Butt</span><a href="#top">Back to the beginning ↑</a></footer>
